WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:06.530
At this point we want to start talking about fractions and a fraction is something that looks like this.

00:06.550 --> 00:11.980
So we would say this fraction is one over two and this fraction is five over six.

00:12.010 --> 00:17.530
We could also say that this fraction represents one half and this fraction represents 5/6.

00:17.950 --> 00:23.200
The first thing you want to know about fractions is that we always call the top number the numerator,

00:23.200 --> 00:26.230
and we always call the bottom number the denominator.

00:26.350 --> 00:30.820
And in a fraction, the top number is always divided by the denominator.

00:30.820 --> 00:36.610
So this line in between the numerator and the denominator means division, or it represents division.

00:36.610 --> 00:43.900
So this fraction one over two also means one divided by two, and this fraction five over six also means

00:43.900 --> 00:45.700
five divided by six.

00:45.730 --> 00:51.580
With that in mind, remember that we can never divide by zero, which means that the denominator of

00:51.580 --> 00:55.470
a fraction can never be zero, because if the denominator were zero.

00:55.480 --> 01:03.040
So for instance, if instead of one over two we had one over zero, that would mean one divided by zero.

01:03.040 --> 01:04.690
We would be dividing by zero.

01:04.690 --> 01:05.860
And we can't do that.

01:05.860 --> 01:10.990
That breaks a rule in math, so we can never have zero in the denominator.

01:10.990 --> 01:14.470
So we never write zero in the denominator.

01:14.650 --> 01:20.020
Not only do fractions represent division, but they also represent parts of a whole.

01:20.020 --> 01:23.320
So we want to think about the numerator as parts.

01:23.910 --> 01:27.480
And we want to think about the denominator as a whole.

01:27.990 --> 01:32.130
So the easiest way to imagine this is to imagine something like a pizza.

01:32.160 --> 01:38.870
Let's say that I order a pizza and will show it as just a round pizza like this.

01:38.880 --> 01:47.580
The whole let's say I'm going to divide into six parts, so I'm going to cut this pizza into six pieces.

01:47.580 --> 01:50.010
So that might look something like this.

01:50.400 --> 01:53.940
I'm going to cut it into six equally sized pieces.

01:53.940 --> 01:55.770
And I didn't do a perfect job drawing this.

01:55.770 --> 01:59.820
But let's say that each of these pieces has an equal size.

02:00.000 --> 02:08.720
Then we have six pieces one, two, three, four, five and six equally sized pieces.

02:08.730 --> 02:14.130
So six pieces make up the entire pizza or six pieces make up the whole.

02:14.310 --> 02:23.100
If I eat five of the six pieces leaving only one piece, then I've eaten 5/6 of the pizza, or I've

02:23.100 --> 02:24.840
eaten five out of the six pieces.

02:24.840 --> 02:30.930
And I would express the amount of the pizza that I've eaten as this fraction here, five over six.

02:31.050 --> 02:35.900
If I eat one out of the six pieces, I would write that as one over six.

02:35.910 --> 02:40.580
If I eat two out of the six pieces, I would write that as two over six.

02:40.590 --> 02:44.880
If I eat four out of the six pieces, I would write that as four over six.

02:44.880 --> 02:47.760
If I eat five of them, I would write five over six.

02:47.760 --> 02:50.970
So that's giving you the idea of parts of a whole.

02:51.150 --> 02:52.200
Think about it this way.

02:52.200 --> 02:57.960
Also, if I eat one out of the six pieces, that means I have five of them remaining.

02:57.960 --> 03:00.680
So I have five over six pieces remaining.

03:00.690 --> 03:05.010
If I eat two, I have four left for the six left.

03:05.010 --> 03:10.260
So my remaining pizza is four over six or 4/6 of the pizza.

03:10.260 --> 03:15.060
If I eat four of the pieces, I have two out of the six pieces remaining.

03:15.420 --> 03:24.090
So these are the number of eaten pieces and these are the number of remaining pieces.

03:24.690 --> 03:29.970
And you'll notice that they always add to six out of the six total pieces.

03:29.970 --> 03:35.970
So if I eat four and I have two remaining, if I add those together, four plus two is six, I get the

03:35.970 --> 03:40.320
total six out of six pieces that represent the entire pizza.

03:40.320 --> 03:46.290
So all that to say, you want to imagine every fraction as parts of a whole where the numerator represents

03:46.290 --> 03:49.050
the parts and the denominator represents the whole.

03:49.290 --> 03:53.940
The only other points we want to make here are that you'll often see fractions written this way with

03:53.940 --> 03:57.690
the numerator above the denominator, but we'll also write fractions this way.

03:57.690 --> 04:03.930
So instead of one over two written this way, we'll write it as one over two like this in line.

04:03.930 --> 04:09.660
If we're writing it, for example, in the middle of a paragraph five over six, we can also write as

04:09.840 --> 04:13.080
five over six with this forward slash like this.

04:13.080 --> 04:15.780
So five over six is equal to five over six.

04:15.780 --> 04:18.330
These are both fractions representing the same thing.

04:18.330 --> 04:20.160
They're just written different ways.

04:20.160 --> 04:25.590
And then the last thing that we want to note here is that fractions are closely related to the concept

04:25.590 --> 04:28.650
of percent, which you'll know from real life.

04:28.650 --> 04:35.070
When you hear percent, for example, 30%, you always want to think about the denominator as being

04:35.070 --> 04:35.640
100.

04:35.640 --> 04:45.570
So when we say 30%, what that really means is 30 in the numerator, divided by 100 in the denominator.

04:45.570 --> 04:49.140
So when you hear percent, you always put 100 in the denominator.

04:49.140 --> 04:53.070
So 30% is equal to the fraction, 30 over 100.

04:53.460 --> 05:01.290
Or as another example, let's say 57%, you know that that's equal to 57 in the numerator divided by

05:01.290 --> 05:02.850
100 in the denominator.

05:02.850 --> 05:09.270
So if you here percent, that means the denominator is 100 and the numerator is whatever number you

05:09.270 --> 05:11.100
were told was the percent.

05:11.100 --> 05:17.640
And we'll talk more later about how to convert back and forth between fractions and percents as well

05:17.640 --> 05:18.930
as decimals.
